# Files that must never enter the container image.
#
# The first entry is the important one: .env holds your real API key and
# encryption secrets. A container image is copied to a registry and pulled onto
# machines, so anything baked into it should be assumed public. Production
# secrets are injected at runtime with `fly secrets set` instead.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
tests/
docs/
.git/
.gitignore
*.md
.DS_Store
